 "items": [
  {
   "ref": "page:migration",
   "type": "page",
   "slug": "moving-from-wordpress",
   "replace": [
    {
     "old": "Teme is in alpha. Import into a test site, read the report, and follow the build.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Import into a copy of your site first, read the report, then move the live site."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "ref": "page:developers",
   "type": "page",
   "slug": "developers",
   "replace": [
    {
     "old": "A preview until Teme 1.0: each change is named in the changelog.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Each change to it is named in the changelog."
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "old": "Each task goes in the smallest place that fits it. Small ones are data that Teme draws, so they look native; larger ones are the plugin’s own screens inside Teme’s frame. Today a plugin adds settings, Tools links and status banners; the rest arrive with the next releases of the plugin API.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Each task goes in the smallest place that fits it. Small ones are data that Teme draws, so they look native; larger ones are the plugin’s own screens inside Teme’s frame. A plugin can have its own area in the admin, with pages, tables, record forms, charts and actions, add panels to the editor and columns to the content lists, and keep its own settings."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "ref": "page:faq",
   "type": "page",
   "slug": "faq",
   "replace": [
    {
     "old": "Not yet. Teme is in alpha, at 0.7.0-alpha.1, and runs only on test sites. Version 1.0 is the first release meant for anyone to install. Follow the build on GitHub to see each release.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Yes. Teme 1.x is a stable release line, made for any publication to install and run. This site runs Teme {{release}}. Every release and its notes are under "
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Releases",
        "marks": [
         {
          "type": "link",
          "attrs": {
           "href": "https://github.com/temecms/teme/releases"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": " on GitHub."
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "old": "Teme has a read-only API, off until you turn it on, for sites and apps that read your content. Writing through an API is not built.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Teme has a read-only API, off until you turn it on, for sites and apps that read your content. A management API lets outside tools sign in with a key to upload media and create, publish and schedule content, each key acting as one person with only the abilities it is given."
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "old": "The foundation is built: every item has a language, and translations are linked. The screens to manage languages come in a later release.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Yes. Every item has a language and translations are linked. Settings › Languages sets the site’s languages, the editor’s Translations section links an item’s versions, and readers get each page in its language."
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "old": "Questions and problems: open an issue on GitHub, when Teme is public.",
     "new": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Questions and problems: open an issue on "
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "GitHub",
        "marks": [
         {
          "type": "link",
          "attrs": {
           "href": "https://github.com/temecms"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
